(*
expect:
absent nil
cell 11
cell holding nil nil
stream #STREAM
stream did not raise
after a stream read the caller keeps going
finished
*)
(* rete#25 — `Channel>>peekCell:ifStream:`, the cell read for a leaf WHOSE KIND
   THE READER DOES NOT CONTROL.

   `peek:` raises `'not a cell'` on a stream leaf. That is right for a reader
   that owns the name, and it is a trap for one that does not: kind is pinned by
   the FIRST write and re-created by replay, so one wrongly kinded write disables
   the reader permanently, with no recovery short of a new path. And the visible
   symptom is worse than a crash — a reader inside a space reaction runs under
   `protectedFire:`, which catches the raise and abandons the REST of the
   reaction's body, so everything after the read silently stops happening on
   every tick while everything before it keeps working. Nothing is logged.
   PortaBridge reading gateway-written `goal/apps/main` is exactly that reader.

   The three kinds get three answers and all three are asserted, because the
   interesting bug is a guard that collapses two of them: nil for a leaf nobody
   has written, the value for a real cell, and the BLOCK for a stream. A cell
   holding nil is asked separately from an absent one for the reason
   `peek:ifAbsent:` already documents — the kind, not the value, says whether the
   pigeonhole is empty, and these two answer the same `nil` by different routes.

   The last two lines are the whole point restated as behaviour: no handler is
   installed anywhere in this test, so a stream leaf reaching the reader has to
   be an ANSWER. Under `peek:` the statements after the stream read would never
   execute. *)
class PeekCellIfStream packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space seen |
    space:: platform space.

    ('absent ' , (space peekCell: 'goal/never/written' ifStream: [ #STREAM ]) printString) println.

    space put: 'goal/apps/main' value: 11.
    ('cell ' , (space peekCell: 'goal/apps/main' ifStream: [ #STREAM ]) printString) println.

    space put: 'goal/held/nil' value: nil.
    ('cell holding nil ' , (space peekCell: 'goal/held/nil' ifStream: [ #STREAM ]) printString) println.

    (* A gateway can create this leaf as a stream — `porta put --raw --kind
       stream` writes one, and applyEntry: applies kind 1 with `out:value:`. *)
    space out: 'goal/wrong/kind' value: 'surprise'.
    seen:: space peekCell: 'goal/wrong/kind' ifStream: [ #STREAM ].
    ('stream ' , seen printString) println.
    'stream did not raise' println.
    'after a stream read the caller keeps going' println.

    'finished' println.
  )
) : (
)
